{"content":[{"text":"[external_agent_tool_call: Bash]\ndescription: Document Scalar in the README\ncommand: cd $HOME/projects/slide-engine; python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md';s=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"Arrow keys continue the presentation. Returning to the component preserves its current tree\"\ni=s.index(anchor)\nend=s.index(\"\\n\",s.index(\"check-serializer.mjs --packaged\",i))+1\ndoc = \"\"\"\n\n`<Scalar />` minimizes the park into `gitviz`, an SGI-style 3D object store\nvisualizer. It takes no children; the demonstration it replays is fixed:\n\n```mdx\n<Scalar title=\"3D Object Store Visualizer\" />\n```\n\nThe ground is divided into three spaces: two users and the shared remote. Six\nsteps walk one metadata store across them. user1 writes commit C1 with tree T1\nlisting `k1→A` and `k2→B`; a second commit re-lists those keys and adds `k3→C`\nand `k4→D` with two new blobs; a prune writes a third commit whose tree keeps\nonly the tip keys, without writing blobs; a push copies every object to the\nremote; user2's setup fetches all commits and trees but only the tip tree's\nblobs; and reading `k1` fetches blob A alone. The command band above the\nviewport shows the `git meta` command each step runs, and the line below it\ndescribes the object that step produced.\n\nRight advances one step and Left steps back, so each step is its own arrow\npress and counts toward Power; Right after the last step continues the\npresentation, and Left on the first step returns to the previous slide. The\nsidebar repeats these as buttons alongside **reset** (R), **play** (Enter),\n**birds eye** (Up) and **front view** (Down); the Steps list jumps directly to\nany step. Tilt and Height aim the camera, Speed sets the pace of automatic\nplayback, and clicking an object inspects it. Objects written by the current\nstep glow and are drawn in orange, including their pointers.\n\nBlob, tree and commit IDs are real Git object IDs computed by the compiler:\ntrees are hashed from their `100644 <key>` entries and commits carry real\nparent lines, so the visualizer's history hashes the way the repository would.\nThe status bar counts distinct objects and the pointers between the objects\ncurrently on the ground. Run `node scripts/check-scalar.mjs` to exercise the\nnative window after building.\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:end]+doc+s[end:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ntail -32 README.md | head -8\n[/external_agent_tool_call]","type":"output_text"}],"event_id":"01a09493-9fb3-7940-8858-80b0243ebd64:292","role":"assistant","session_id":"01a09493-9fb3-7940-8858-80b0243ebd64","source_line":292,"timestamp":"2026-09-12T07:44:57.809Z","type":"message"}
