{"content":[{"text":"Done. The `<Scalar />` component is implemented end to end and verified in the running app.\n\n**What it does.** `<Scalar />` is a standalone MDX step that minimizes the park into `gitviz`, an SGI-style 3D object store visualizer. The ground holds three spaces, two users and a shared remote, and six steps walk one metadata store across them: user1 writes commit C1 with tree T1 listing k1 and k2; a second commit re-lists those and adds k3 and k4 with two new blobs; a prune writes a third commit whose tree keeps only the tip keys and writes no blobs; a push copies everything to the remote; user2's setup pulls all commits and trees but only the tip tree's blobs; and reading k1 fetches blob A alone. Each step shows the `git meta` command it runs, taken from the CLI in the neighbouring git-meta repo.\n\n**Files added.**\n- `src/scalar.mjs` generates the scenario, hashing real Git blob, tree and parent-linked commit IDs.\n- `unreal/Source/SlideEngine/ParkScalar.{h,cpp}`, `ParkScalarView.cpp`, `ParkScalarWindow.cpp`, `ParkScalarInteraction.cpp` hold the state, the projected 3D view, the window chrome and the smoke test.\n- `scripts/check-scalar.mjs`, `test/scalar.test.mjs`, `examples/git-meta/scalar.mdx`.\n\n**Files changed.** The compiler registry, the desktop lifecycle in `ParkCommandDesktop.cpp`, page handling and Power scoring in `ParkStationContent.cpp`, the desktop overlay in `ParkLogin.cpp`, key handling in `ParkNavigation.cpp`, the game mode header, README, and the rebuilt `unreal/Content/Slides/deck.json`.\n\n**Controls.** Right and Left walk the steps, so each is its own arrow press and counts toward Power. The sidebar adds reset, play, birds eye and front view with Tilt, Height and Speed sliders, a Steps list and a legend. Clicking an object inspects it; objects written by the current step glow orange along with their pointers.\n\n**Verified.** 23 node tests pass, the Unreal module builds, and the new interaction check passes all 12 assertions in the packaged game. The existing FSV, Serializer and station checks still pass.\n\nI left everything uncommitted. Several files in this worktree, README.md included, already carry other agents' edits, so committing whole files would sweep their work in. Tell me if you want a session branch and I will commit only the hunks that are mine.","type":"output_text"}],"event_id":"01a09493-9fb3-7940-8858-80b0243ebd64:300","role":"assistant","session_id":"01a09493-9fb3-7940-8858-80b0243ebd64","source_line":300,"timestamp":"2026-09-12T07:44:57.809Z","type":"message"}
