{"content":[{"text":"Yes. The computer is the 1990s workstation used by the `Computer` component, and it is a real modeled asset, not a sprite.\n\n- **Source of truth** is `scripts/model_terminal.py`, which builds the monitor, tapered CRT housing, bezels, keyboard and a sticky note procedurally in Blender.\n- **Editable scene** is `assets/blender/park.blend`. The build script executes the terminal model and writes it into that file, so there is no separate terminal blend.\n- **Rebuild** it with `scripts/build_park_assets.py` through Blender, then import with `scripts/import_park_assets.py`.\n- **Render for review** sits at `assets/blender/terminal-review.png`, produced by `scripts/review_terminal.py`.\n- **In the game** it loads as `SM_Terminal` from the Park models content folder, spawned by `ParkTerminal.cpp`.\n\nNote the other on-screen hardware differs. Cold storage has its own blend and script, while the wooden signs, clipboard and the new gitviz window are drawn natively rather than modeled.","type":"output_text"}],"event_id":"01a09493-9fb3-7940-8858-80b0243ebd64:356","role":"assistant","session_id":"01a09493-9fb3-7940-8858-80b0243ebd64","source_line":356,"timestamp":"2026-09-12T07:44:57.810Z","type":"message"}
